  "description": "The page is exactly full and the file is exactly exhausted, which separates two arms a fuller file conflates. Seven records satisfy IF WS-SCRN-COUNTER = WS-MAX-SCREEN-LINES at :1191, so :1194-1195 stores the seventh record as the page's last key and the look-ahead READNEXT at :1197 is issued anyway - learning whether an eighth record exists is that read's only purpose. It returns DFHRESP(ENDFILE), so :1215-1216 sets CA-NEXT-PAGE-NOT-EXISTS and :1218-1221 moves 'NO MORE RECORDS TO SHOW', leaving the seventh record's key standing because the ENDFILE arm overwrites nothing. The info line is still informed: :917 matches, and :926-929's second condition only suppresses the text for the no-records message, which this is not. So the operator sees both lines - contrast case04, where one is suppressed.",
